#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5
#: using-mainwindow-timelineview.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Timeline View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: using-mainwindow-timelineview.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Timeline View shows a timescale-adjustable histogram of the numbers of "
"images per time unit which is selectable by a drop down field. To the right "
"of that you can choose between a linear or logarithmic histogram. A "
"selection frame moves over the histogram. To display the photographs out of "
"a certain time frame just click on the corresponding bar. You are not "
"restricted to one bar. With <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;"
"<mousebutton>left</mousebutton></keycombo> click or <keycombo action=\"simul"
"\">&Ctrl;<mousebutton>left</mousebutton></keycombo> click you can add more "
"bars to the first one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5
#: using-mainwindow-timelineview.docbook:16
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the field right below you can enter a title and save your selection. It "
"will then appear in the <quote>Searches</quote> list field below. But the "
"best is still to come: the Timeline View offers a search for a search! If "
"you have a lot more searches saved than my ridiculous four in the screenshot "
"the adaptive search field at the bottom may help to find a certain search."
msgstr ""
